From c168680abde1c655faabf80068273ef61c36e38b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:08:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(odo): stop fabricating findings; replace paid sources
 with native code
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ODO was reporting security gaps it had never checked. Three separate bugs,
all of which reached the client report:

1. Email security ran through MXToolbox, and with no MXTOOLBOX_API_KEY set it
   returned { spf: false, dkim: false, dmarc: false } — so every scan told the
   prospect they had no email authentication at all. DKIM was additionally
   hardcoded false even when the key was present, so it was never checked.
2. calculateSecurityScore deducted for any source returning null, including
   ones that had no key wired. A prospect with perfect email security scored
   the same as one with none — a systematic penalty of roughly 40 points on
   every scan.
3. VirusTotal was live in the research path. Its Public API terms forbid use
   "in commercial products or services", which ODO is. Removed, not disabled.

The root cause is that a boolean cannot express "we did not manage to check".
Introduces odo-evidence.ts with three states — observed / absent /
not_determined — and the rule that only a confirmed absence may be scored as a
gap or trigger a service match. DNS timeouts and WAF 403s now resolve to
not_determined with a reason, and coverage is surfaced to the reviewer so an
incomplete scan reads as an ODO problem rather than bad news about the client.

Verified against live domains: microsoft.com and shopify.com both returned
spf=NOT_DETERMINED(ETIMEOUT) under a degraded resolver. Both publish SPF. The
old code would have reported them as having none.

Sources removed (see odo-research.ts header for the terms on each):
  VirusTotal     — commercial use prohibited by their API terms
  HaveIBeenPwned — breacheddomain only answers for domains you own
  Shodan         — free accounts have no host-lookup API access
  BuiltWith      — $295/month, replaced by native fingerprinting
  Hunter.io      — 25 searches/month; inbound ODO has no contact to discover
  MXToolbox      — replaced by native DNS, which also returns real DKIM
  SecurityHeaders.io — replaced by reading response headers directly

New native modules, no vendor and no key:
  odo-dns.ts  — SPF with qualifier strength, DMARC with policy grading
                (p=none is the finding, not the absence of DMARC), DKIM across
                8 platform selectors, mail platform with security-gateway
                detection, definitive Microsoft 365 tenant detection via the
                openid-configuration endpoint, NS delegation (identifies the
                incumbent IT provider), CAA/MTA-STS/TLS-RPT/BIMI.
  odo-page.ts — tech-stack fingerprinting across 45 signatures, on-page SEO
                health, and well-known file checks, all from one page fetch.

MX records alone are not sufficient for M365 detection: Mimecast, Proofpoint
and Barracuda proxy the mail flow and mask the mailbox provider entirely.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
